# Never commit game files or binaries — this project stores only files we create.
# Game executables, assets, and archives
*.exe
*.dll
*.bin
# RenderWare engine package/asset formats (original game content)
*.dff
*.txd
*.rws
# Extracted or dumped memory / process data
*.dmp
*.dump
*.raw
# Local scratch
/tmp/
*.log

# ...EXCEPT recon evidence, which IS the finding rather than scratch.
#
# Added 2026-09-14 across the estate. The blanket log rule above was
# silently swallowing recon captures: `git add` on an ignored file succeeds
# with no error and no output, so a session that believed it had saved its
# evidence got no signal that it had not. On dead-space-2-vr that cost the
# sole proof of the camera finding, and two other repos had already patched
# themselves without the lesson spreading.
#
# Text logs only. Dumps and binaries stay ignored ON PURPOSE - a memory dump
# can be hundreds of MB and would break the repo or carry game content. When
# evidence is too big to commit, say so loudly in the write-up instead.
!recon/**/*.log
